"""Shared finer mesh and provenance findings for both living reports."""
import json

def add_v24(d,P,new_page,para,table,picture):
 O=P/'engineering-v24-results'
 if not (O/'review_status.json').exists():return
 r=json.loads((O/'review_status.json').read_text())
 new_page(d,'V24 Finer child and adult joint calculations')
 para(d,'24 October 2026. We added a finer 1.5 mm target mesh for both isolated joint families. There are four new equilibrium calculations, covering outward and inward loads on child large and adult small. The V19 part shapes and corrected virtual spacer equations are unchanged. These are new meshes of an existing mathematical reference, not new headphone designs.')
 table(d,['Joint family','Load direction','Mesh nodes','Relative force error'],[[x['size'].replace('_',' '),x['direction'],str((len(x['rigid_motion_controls']) and json.loads((O/(x['size']+'_mesh_trial.json')).read_text())['nodes'])),format(x['independent_residual'],'.2e')] for x in r['cases']],[2.0,1.55,1.35,2.0])
 para(d,'All four new fields meet the chosen equilibrium, independent residual, net force, net moment, friction bound and contact derivative checks. Common rigid motion checks also pass. The old displacement fields were mapped only to help the solver start; the mapped values were not accepted as a solution. Each final field had to meet the force residual gate.')
 para(d,'The assumptions remain stiffness 3500 MPa, Poisson ratio 0.35, preload 140 N, friction 0.2 and a side force of plus or minus 2 N. The virtual spacer is 0.5 mm. This model still omits a resolved real washer, bolt, material history, full headset loading and worn contact. The complete raw fields, histories and hashes are saved.')
 new_page(d,'V24 Do the finer stress predictions agree')
 picture(d,'V24_finer_comparison','Same corrected reference equations and stress sampling sets on 1.9 mm and 1.5 mm target meshes. The dashed line is our chosen 5 percent comparison limit, not a product safety standard.',6.55)
 para(d,str(r['stress_comparison_passes'])+' of 16 refined stress comparisons meet the chosen 5 percent limit. Eight comparisons use 125 interior samples per element and eight use a 35 point set including boundaries. All comparisons use the same method on the older and newer mesh. Earlier V23 comparisons remain unchanged in the history.')
 para(d,'The finer child results still exceed the limit. This shows that the coarse mesh was not the only unresolved issue. It does not by itself identify the physical cause. A single passing pair would also not prove the maximum stress throughout a part. We have not changed the limit or replaced a failed peak criterion with average stress. Reliable whole part strength remains unproved.')
 para(d,'Further useful work needs the intended physical edge, contact, spacer and fastener details to be defined and represented. More fine meshes of an incomplete contact idealization cannot prove the finished device is strong, comfortable or quiet. No CAD shape or final material is selected by these calculations.')
 new_page(d,'V24 Restored records and the remaining software gates')
 para(d,'Moving to D revealed that the main CAD readers still followed old C drive paths. They now resolve a source using its recorded hash. An audit matched all 623 recorded references, covering 304 distinct path and hash pairs. Four older V12 versions did not match the newer root files; exact copies were recovered from existing ZIP archives into a separate source archive. The newer files and historical recorded paths were preserved.')
 table(d,['Recovered historical source','Recovery rule'],[['V12 child small released','Exact recorded SHA256 required'],['V12 child small folded','Exact recorded SHA256 required'],['V12 child medium released','Exact recorded SHA256 required'],['V12 child medium folded','Exact recorded SHA256 required']],[3.9,3.0])
 para(d,'Seven path loader controls passed, including rejection of a deliberately wrong hash. This fixes the two primary mesh and motion readers. It does not claim that every historical script has been migrated or that every CAD shape has passed every geometric test. The eight V23 raw solution files also remain unchanged.')
 table(d,['Area','Remaining requirement'],[['Joint strength','Define actual edge spacer fastener and loads then resolve stress reliability'],['Cushion contact','Traceable foam curves cover seams friction and worn head geometry'],['Sony compatibility','Exact skirt groove carrier dimensions and tolerances'],['Sound heat and durability','Material and assembly inputs for predictive full product models'],['Comfort and sensory acceptance','Voluntary wearer testing']],[2.1,4.8])
 para(d,'Both products remain in development. The glasses cushion geometry is unchanged; these shared joint and source checks add no Sony fit, pain relief, sound leakage, ANC or cooling result. This finer numerical campaign is complete, but full product software sign off is not achieved. The test register records failed and missing requirements explicitly.')
